{"additions":261,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3Mzk0MjAw","is_bot":false,"login":"BagToad","name":"Kynan Ware"},"baseRefName":"trunk","changedFiles":10,"closedAt":"2026-11-07T01:48:47Z","deletions":18,"headRefName":"bagtoad/triage-ghmock-skill","isDraft":false,"latestReviews":[{"id":"","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nFixture URL validation captures adjacent non-URL content, incorrectly blocking publication for valid URLs in compact JSON and adjacent Markdown links.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>1 open issue</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Validate fixture URLs independently of surrounding content](https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/14976#discussion_r4499039797) · New\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>What changed in this PR</strong></summary>\n\nThis PR introduces `example.invalid` as the synthetic repository owner so triage reports can publish fixture URLs without live repository lookups. It addresses publication failures, not the CODEOWNERS behavior in #9604.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Exempts the synthetic owner from visibility checks and adds fixture-path validation.\n- Updates ghmock defaults, examples, and reproduction guidance.\n- Adds coverage for fixture publication, visibility checks, and synthetic Git remotes.\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| `script/​ghmock/​scaffold_test.go` | Updates expected scaffold repository names and URLs. |\r\n| `script/​ghmock/​main.go` | Documents the synthetic namespace in command help. |\r\n| `script/​ghmock/​gqlscaffold.go` | Uses shared synthetic repository placeholders. |\r\n| `script/​ghmock/​gitcmd_test.go` | Covers synthetic repository parsing, creation, and cloning. |\r\n| `docs/​issue-triage.md` | Explains fixture exemptions and visibility requirements. |\r\n| `.github/​workflows/​issue-triage.md` | Updates reproduction instructions for synthetic repositories. |\r\n| `.github/​workflows/​issue-triage.lock.yml` | Refreshes the generated workflow body hash. |\r\n| `.github/​skills/​ghmock/​SKILL.md` | Aligns fixture guidance and examples with the namespace. |\r\n| `.github/​scripts/​issue-triage-report.test.cjs` | Adds publication and fixture-path validation cases. |\r\n| `.github/​scripts/​issue-triage-report.cjs` | Adds the synthetic-owner exemption and URL validation. |\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>","submittedAt":"2026-11-07T00:23:11Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":""}},{"id":"","author":{"login":"tidy-dev"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-11-07T01:27:26Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"APPROVED","commit":{"oid":""}}],"mergeStateStatus":"UNKNOWN","mergeable":"UNKNOWN","mergedAt":"2026-11-07T01:48:47Z","number":14976,"reviewDecision":"APPROVED","state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-11-07T01:44:07Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/cli/cli/actions/runs/42325466453/job/128259599242","name":"CodeQL-Build (go, manual, ./.github/codeql/codeql-config.yml)","startedAt":"2026-11-07T01:42:06Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Code Scanning"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-11-07T01:44:36Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/cli/cli/actions/runs/42325466445/job/128259599765","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-11-07T01:42:06Z","status":"COM